n location\" — the entity producing = manufacturer. I'll include, and it matches revision 3 \"Added second production location\". I'll keep role implicit via manufacturers list. Fine.\n\n**certified_type**: category \"Water meter\", type_designations [\"WATERFLUX 3070\"], description \"An electromagnetic water meter\".\n\nWait — category examples in schema: \"Load cell\", \"Indicator\", \"Measuring system\", \"Fuel dispenser\", \"Taximeter\", \"Gas meter\"... So \"Water meter\" fits pattern.\n\n**recommendation.accuracy_classes**: [\"1\", \"2\"].\n\nNow software matrix table name: \"Software versions and CRC checksums\". Rows:\n- {software_version: \"4.0.4_\", crc_checksum: \"Not applicable\"}\n- 4.0.10_, 4.0.11_, 4.0.12_, 4.2.2_, 4.2.4_, 4.2.5_, 4.2.6_, 4.3.0_, 4.3.1_ → Not applicable\n- 5.0.1_ → \"4Cb5\"\n- 5.0.2_ → \"71d5\"\n- 5.0.3_ → \"CFF7\"\n- 5.0.5_ → \"dCAb\"\n- 5.1.0_ → \"Ab62\"\n\nKeep the trailing underscore as in doc (software version format \"5.0.1_\"). Yes, keep as-is.\n\nNow, config entries for power supply. Let me finalize:\n\nconfig_level entries:\n\n1. environmental_class, axis \"software_version\":\n   - {condition: \"software version 5.0.1_ or higher\", value: \"O (installed outdoors)\"}\n   - {condition: \"software version 4.3.1_ or lower\", value: \"B (installed in a building)\"}\n\n2. temperature_range_ambient, axis \"software_version\":\n   - {condition: \"software version 5.0.1_ or higher\", value: {min: -25, max: 55}, unit_symbol: \"°C\"}\n   - {condition: \"software version 4.3.1_ or lower\", value: {min: -10, max: 55}, unit_symbol: \"°C\"}\n\n3. field_current, axis \"software_version\":\n   - {condition: \"software version 4.3.1_ or lower (only value possible)\", value: 16, unit_symbol: \"mA\"}\n   - {condition: \"software version 5.0.1_ or higher (selectable; shall be set to 16 mA)\", value: 16, unit_symbol: \"mA\"}\n\n4. power_supply, axis \"software_version\":\n   - {condition: \"all software versions\", value: \"3.6 V D-cell Lithium 