- electromagnetic_environment: {value: \"E2\"}\n- water_temperature_class: {value: \"T50\"}\n- water_temperature_range: {value: {min: 0.1, max: 50}, unit_symbol: \"°C\"} — from \"T50 (+0,1 °C / +50 °C)\". Note the \"+0,1\" — water temp min 0.1 °C (cold potable). Convert 0,1→0.1. Good.\n- maximum_admissible_pressure: {value: 1.6, unit_symbol: \"MPa\"}\n- maximum_admissible_pressure_bar — skip? I'll include \"maximum_admissible_pressure_alternative\": {value: 16, unit_symbol: \"bar\"}. Hmm. I'll include it — more data preserved, low cost. Actually rule: pure units not values; this is a real value. Keep both. Name: \"maximum_admissible_pressure_equivalent\"? I'll use \"maximum_admissible_pressure_alt\" hmm. Let me just include one: \"maximum_admissible_pressure\": 1.6 MPa, and \"maximum_admissible_pressure_bar\": 16 bar. Eh, \"maximum_admissible_pressure_bar\" as label is odd. Use \"maximum_admissible_pressure_equivalent_in_bar\"? Too long. I'll do value 1.6 MPa only and skip bar (it's just unit conversion). Decision: skip bar.\n\nHmm, actually many extractors would keep both. I'll keep just MPa. Fine.\n\n- orientation: {value: \"All positions (horizontal, vertical or diagonal)\"}\n- flow_profile_sensitivity_class: {value: \"U0 and D0\"}\n- flow_profile_sensitivity_note / straight_length: {value: \"0 x DN upstream and 0 x DN downstream\"}? I'll include attribute \"straight_length_requirement\": {value: \"0 x DN upstream and 0 x DN downstream\"}. Good—separate from class.\n- reverse_flow: {value: \"The sensor is designed to measure reverse flow\"}\n- pressure_loss_class: {value: \"Δp 63\"} — keep \"Δp 63\" as string; avoid LaTeX issues — Δ is fine unicode.\n- maximum_pressure_loss: {value: 0.63, unit_symbol: \"bar\"}\n\nThat's type_level.\n\nNow let me also think: does \"Accuracy class 1 and 2\" belong in recommendation.accuracy_classes — yes [\"1\",\"2\"].\n\nOutput JSON structure. Let me now write it fully.\n\nAlso models[].label: e.g. \"WATERFLUX 3070 DN25, class 2, Q3 = 10 m³/h\". \n\nmodel_family.family_name: \"WATERFLUX 3070\".\n\nLet me write model entries compactly:\n\nFor each model: {\"model_id\": \"DN25-class2-Q3=10\", \"label\": \"DN25, class 2, Q3 = 10 m³/h\", \"attributes\": {\"meter_size\": \"DN25\", \"accuracy_class\": \"2\", \"indicating_range\": {\"value\": 99999999, \"unit_symbol\": \"m³\"}, \"verification_scale_interval_maximum\": {\"value\": 0.0001, \"unit_symbol\": \"m³\"}}}\n\n36 of these. VSI by group as computed.\n\nLet me assign VSI:\n- DN25 (2 models), DN40 (2), DN50 (2): 0.0001\n- DN65 (3), DN80 (4), DN100 (4), DN125 (4), DN150 (4): 0.001\n- DN200 (2), DN250 (2), DN300 (2), DN350 (1), DN400 (1), DN450 (1): 0.01\n- DN500 (1), DN600 (1): 0.1\n\nOK. Now the matrix_tables flow rows: same 36 rows with values.\n\nColumn units: q1..q4 m³/h. I'll include \"column_units\" array in matrix table like the R137 example. \n\nRow object keys: model_id, meter_size, accuracy_class, q1, q2, q3, q4, ratio_q3_q1.\n\nNow assemble JSON. Careful with valid JSON (no trailing commas). Also ensure no LaTeX. The \"Δp\" character is fine.\n\nAlso \"temperature_range_ambient\" — value {min:-25,max:55}. \n\nAlso note: The note about field current \"can only be set to 16 mA\" / \"shall be set to 16 mA\" — value 16 mA both; conditions capture semantics.\n\nRevision history:\n[\n {\"revision\": \"Initial\", \"date\": \"2021-01-26\", \"changes\": null},\n {\"revision\": \"1\", \"date\": \"2022-05-03\", \"changes\": \"Added alternative Modbus PCB components\"},\n {\"revision\": \"2\", \"date\": \"2023-06-12\", \"changes\": \"Added Alternative Micro Controller Unit (MCU)\"},\n {\"revision\": \"3\", \"date\": \"2024-07-30\", \"changes\": \"Added second production location\"}\n]\n\nTest reports:\n[\n {\"id\": \"R49-1/2006-NL1-09.01\", \"date\": \"2009-09-16\", \"pages\": 41, \"role\": \"type_evaluation_report\"},\n {\"id\": \"R49-1/2006-NL1-10.01\", \"date\": \"2010-04-09\", \"pages\": 40, \"role\": \"type_evaluation_report\"},\n {\"id\": \